# Copy to .env.local and fill in. Never commit a filled-in copy.

# Neon Postgres. DATABASE_URL is the pooled connection used for normal queries;
# DATABASE_URL_UNPOOLED is the unpooled one, required for LISTEN/NOTIFY (SSE) and
# for drizzle-kit migrations. See REQUIREMENTS.md § 6.
# Locally both point at the docker-compose database:
#   pnpm db:up && pnpm db:migrate
#   postgres://jandh:jandh@localhost:5432/jandh
DATABASE_URL=
DATABASE_URL_UNPOOLED=

# Google OAuth (consent screen in "Testing" mode). REQUIREMENTS.md § 5.1.
GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=

# Comma-separated, lowercase. Login is rejected unless the verified Google email
# matches one of these exactly.
ALLOWED_EMAILS=

# Optional. Turns the email-only development login on or off (REQUIREMENTS.md § 5.4.),
# outranking the default, which is ON under `next dev` and OFF everywhere else. Only
# `true`, `1` or `on` enable it; absent or blank keeps the default.
#
# Set it for a LOCAL production build — `pnpm build && pnpm start` is what § 16.'s
# offline behaviour has to be tested on, and the default there is off. `/login`
# prerenders, so it must be set before `next build` and not just before `next start`.
#
# NEVER set it on a deployment. It signs in any ALLOWED_EMAILS address on an email
# alone, with none of § 5.1.'s Google verification behind it.
ENABLE_DEV_LOGIN=

# ISO YYYY-MM-DD. The calendar D-day counts from here, with the start date
# itself as day 1. REQUIREMENTS.md § 11.1.
RELATIONSHIP_START_DATE=

# Cloudflare R2. Private bucket, public access disabled. REQUIREMENTS.md § 9.
R2_ACCOUNT_ID=
R2_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
R2_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=
R2_BUCKET=

# Absolute origin(s) of this deployment, e.g. http://localhost:3000
# Comma-separated when the same deployment answers under more than one origin
# (a custom domain alongside the platform-assigned one, or mid-migration between
# two domains). The Google OAuth redirect_uri is resolved per-request against this
# list (src/shared/config/app.ts's resolveAppUrl), so every origin listed here must
# also be registered as an authorized redirect URI in the Google Cloud console.
#
# infra/Caddyfile also reads this var, as its site address list — so on the
# self-hosted deploy, separate entries with ", " (comma AND a space), not a bare
# comma. Caddy's Caddyfile tokenizes site addresses on whitespace and only strips
# a trailing comma from each token; a bare comma with no space leaves two domains
# glued into one address that matches neither.
APP_URLS=

# Optional. Origin jandh-emoticons is deployed to. This app rewrites /emoticons/*
# there, so that repo's SCREENS are served same-origin with this one rather than as
# a subdomain (an installed iOS PWA hands a cross-origin link to Safari View
# Controller, which carries none of the web app's cookies).
#
# NEXT_PUBLIC_, because it is read twice: next.config.ts builds the rewrite target
# from it, and the browser builds § 13.8.1.'s keyword-suggester URL from it — that
# one call goes to jandh-emoticons directly, skipping the rewrite hop.
#
# Leave it EMPTY locally — the default is that repo's dev server on port 3001.
# Production sets `https://jandh-emoticons.jeheecheon.com`, with no trailing slash
# and no /emoticons suffix; both readers add the prefix themselves.
NEXT_PUBLIC_EMOTICONS_ORIGIN=

# Optional. Points the emoticon API — packs, items, prefs, upload URLs — at
# jandh-emoticons instead of this app's own routes, so that the emoticon work runs on
# that deployment's budget rather than on this one's (REQUIREMENTS.md § 13.7.1.).
# Only `true`, `1` or `on` turn it on; absent or blank keeps this app's own routes,
# which stay deployed and are what a new environment must fall back to.
#
# It is a switch and NOT an address: the origin comes from
# NEXT_PUBLIC_EMOTICONS_ORIGIN above, so there is no second copy of it to drift.
# That also means this does nothing while that variable is empty — its own default is
# a dev server, and pointing production at localhost:3001 is mixed content the browser
# blocks. Set the origin first, or the switch is ignored.
#
# Turning it on has two prerequisites, and skipping either takes the whole emoticon
# feature down rather than degrading it:
#   1. jandh-emoticons must be DEPLOYED with its CORS routes. A response without
#      those headers is withheld from the browser entirely.
#   2. That deployment must set CORS_ALLOWED_ORIGIN to this app's origin.
#
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ is inlined at build time, so flipping this needs a redeploy of this
# app — editing the variable alone changes nothing about what is already running.
NEXT_PUBLIC_EMOTICON_API_REMOTE=

# Optional. Parent domain the session cookie is issued to, so jandh and
# jandh-emoticons share one login (REQUIREMENTS.md § 5.2.). Production sets
# `.jeheecheon.com`; both deployments must set the same value.
#
# Leave it EMPTY everywhere else. `localhost` accepts no Domain at all, and the
# `pnpm dev:tunnel` funnel answers on `.ts.net`, which shares no registrable domain
# with production — a value set there would be rejected by the browser rather than
# scoped narrowly, and the two sessions cannot reach each other either way.
SESSION_COOKIE_DOMAIN=

# Optional. Turns off the idle close, its 절전 모드 overlay, and the blur close that
# reaches a desktop window sitting behind another one (REQUIREMENTS.md § 8.4.1.).
# Off therefore means such a window stays live and holds a Neon compute awake plus
# a Vercel invocation running for as long as it is open. Leave it unset for the
# default, which is ON — the cheap behaviour has to be opted out of rather than
# remembered. Only false, 0 or off disable it.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SSE_IDLE_SLEEP=

# Optional. How many keyword-suggestion requests one run keeps in flight
# (REQUIREMENTS.md § 13.8.1.). Leave it EMPTY for the default of 6 — an empty value
# is not 1, because every name here ships blank and a copied blank must not quietly
# return the feature to its old sequential speed.
#
# What bounds it is Google's per-minute quota, not this app: the free tier answers
# 15 requests a minute, and a 36-item pack is 12. Lower it if that quota is being
# shared with something else; 1 is the sequential run this replaced.
#
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ is inlined at build time, so changing it needs a redeploy.
NEXT_PUBLIC_KEYWORD_SUGGESTION_CONCURRENCY=

# 공공데이터포털 특일 정보 (한국천문연구원) key. The server reads getRestDeInfo with it at
# runtime and caches the answer for about a month (REQUIREMENTS.md § 11.7.), and
# `pnpm holidays` uses it to refresh src/shared/lib/date/holiday-table.ts, which is
# the fallback the calendar draws whenever that request does not arrive.
#
# Unset, nothing breaks and nothing says so on screen — the fallback is what the
# reader sees, and a `[공휴일]` line in the server log is the only report. Local work
# does not need a key, and `next dev` says so once as info rather than repeating it;
# a deployment does need one, and logs an error on every render until it has one.
#
# WARNING: a data.go.kr key carries a two-year 활용기간 and the gateway refuses every
# call once it lapses. Behind a month-long cache that is a silent death — note the
# expiry date when the key is issued and renew it on the portal before then.
#
# Issue one at https://www.data.go.kr/data/15012690/openapi.do. The portal hands out
# an encoded and a decoded copy of the same key; either works, because the reader
# decodes an encoded copy before percent-encoding it once itself.
DATA_GO_KR_SERVICE_KEY=

# 설정 → 서버 관리 (REQUIREMENTS.md § 12.4.). The three ops jobs run as GitHub Actions
# workflows; the screen's buttons dispatch them, so what this app holds is a token that can
# START a named workflow rather than one that can delete a bucket. It stays server-side —
# the browser never sees it.
#
# A fine-grained PAT scoped to this repository alone, with one permission:
#   Actions: Read and write
#
# Unset, nothing breaks: the backup list and the per-backup deletion read R2 directly and
# work as ever, and 백업 생성 / 삭제 파일 회수 / 고아 파일 정리 are hidden rather than shown
# and then failed.
OPS_GITHUB_TOKEN=
# Both optional. They default to this repository and to `main`, which is the only ref a
# scheduled run ever fires on — set them only for a fork.
# OPS_GITHUB_REPO=GgumiPooh/jandh
# OPS_GITHUB_REF=main

# Optional. Apple Shortcuts (iCloud) download link for sharing shortcut.
# E.g. https://www.icloud.com/shortcuts/xxxxxxxx
NEXT_PUBLIC_SHORTCUT_ICLOUD_URL=

# Web Push (REQUIREMENTS.md § 16.1.). Generate a pair with:
#   node -e "console.log(require('web-push').generateVAPIDKeys())"
# The public key is NEXT_PUBLIC_ because the browser needs it to subscribe; it is
# a public key and safe to ship. VAPID_SUBJECT must be a mailto: or https: URL —
# the push services use it to reach whoever operates this deployment.
NEXT_PUBLIC_VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY=
VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY=
VAPID_SUBJECT=
